# FinTrack API — quick requests (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client)
# Docker compose runs the API on :8080. For local `dotnet run` use :5080.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@email = demo@fintrack.local
@password = Sup3rSecret!

### Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}", "displayName": "Demo User" }

### Login (copy "accessToken" from the response into @token below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List categories (9 defaults are seeded on registration)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a category
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Coffee", "type": "Expense" }

### Create a transaction (replace categoryId with a real id from the categories list)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "Expense",
  "amount": 450,
  "currency": "TRY",
  "categoryId": "REPLACE_WITH_CATEGORY_ID",
  "description": "market shopping",
  "transactionDate": "2026-07-12"
}

### List transactions (filtered, sorted, paged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/transactions?type=Expense&search=market&sortBy=Date&sortDir=Desc&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
